# Network Summary

The HoloJARVIS network architecture is centered around a Raspberry Pi 5 acting as the primary AI server and orchestration node. Desktop, web, and mobile clients communicate securely with the Raspberry Pi through REST APIs and WebSockets. Connected computers run lightweight agents that receive approved commands, execute tasks, and report results. The architecture is designed for scalability, supporting 10 or more managed systems while providing secure remote access, real-time communication, and future expansion into distributed AI, edge computing, and smart home integration.
